I know that this aspect of the discussion is dying down, but I wanted
to add some comments on the subject.  I disagree with all the complaints
about the game being too hard, arbitrary death, etc.  My feelings:

Arbitrary death.  Nonsense.  Ninety-nine percent of the times that I die
is due to my own stupidity or not making the best tactical choice.
Of course, after I die, I know what I should have done.

The game is too hard.  It is certainly tougher than rogue or Nethack 2.3,
but it is quite playable.  I hadn't played nethack for several years,
but I did remember some of the tricks.  Also, a friend of mine and myself
would discover things and discuss the game.  Most of the spoilers on
this newsgroup could be discovered, but by posting them a lot of time
devoted to experimentation is saved; I certainly appreciate them.
Some suggestions:

	- Be patient.  Running around and beating on everything in sight
	  is the quickest way to an early death.  Also, decsend
	  into the dungeon slowly.  Others have said this and this
	  more than anything else is the most important thing to
	  remember while playing.

	- Use explore mode.  Especially, use the wand of wishing that you
	  get to create items for experimenting.  Example, wish for rings
	  of polymorph and polymorph control and play around with
	  becoming various monsters and see what each is like.

	- Until you become more accustomed to the game, play a priest.
	  Knowing whether an item is cursed/normal/blessed is very useful
	  and I like the ability to kick.  Kicking is a very good attack
	  mode and also very effective for opening chests/boxes.  I have
	  actually developed a personal liking for the priest character.

Most of these suggestions are nothing new and have been mentioned by others
in the past, but I consider myself only an 'intermediate level' nethack
player, not an expert.  I only wanted to add some positive comments to the
overwhelming complaints and sense of frustration.  I have some complaints,
but most of them are fairly minor.  I like the improvement with the eating
code in Patch 5, but there do seem to be a few creases that need ironed.

Now a few specific bugs (maybe) in 3.0g Patchlevel 5

    1. No more messages indicating a shop is on the current level. (I think
       Dave Hairston mentioned this one too).

    2. I was, in the words of some kibitzers, "pissing around" with a pile
       of stuff and a wand of polymorph when I created 5 war hammers named
       Mjolnir.  I thought, "awesome", and tried picking them up, but I could
       only carry some of them and picked up 3.  I then dropped some junk
       and poked through the pile and the 2 remaining war hammers were now
       simply listed as '2 war hammers'.  I picked them up and they were
       still listed in my pack as '2 war hammers' and I also had
       '3 war hammers named Mjolnir'

Overall, kudos to the development team for a job well done.

